            {
                "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                "word": "bolter",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "065288c5-fd54-4d50-87c9-98448ae0a5bb",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bolters"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c04fefbd-abac-34ab-8ca3-4e4a5238dfc2",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person or thing that bolts, or runs suddenly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "daa46a87-0b9a-41e4-af29-c85003f14f2e",
                                "sense_id": "c04fefbd-abac-34ab-8ca3-4e4a5238dfc2",
                                "text": "1992 June, Bill Tarrant, Gun Dogs: Problems with a Hunting Pattern, Field & Stream, page 104,\nBolting can be one of the worst problems in dogdom to solve. We′ve all seen a bolter — or rather, we haven't seen him. We released him to hunt, and he was gone for the day, the week, the month. I′ve known of bolters to be gone for years."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "459597ec-cc80-39bc-a927-19e6ff34d03d",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A plant that grows larger and more rapidly than usual."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f5ad266-66ab-47c5-9c44-5f8570d04ff3",
                                "sense_id": "459597ec-cc80-39bc-a927-19e6ff34d03d",
                                "text": "Evidence is accumulating that bolters are plants which have changed their long-day habit to that of short-day."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bb489c8b-c855-334a-8592-0a1ee8c9c6a8",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A machine or mechanism that automatically sifts milled flour."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ca47c6c-ebe8-4a27-8cce-aa1d9439c7cd",
                                "sense_id": "bb489c8b-c855-334a-8592-0a1ee8c9c6a8",
                                "text": "The bolter was basically a sheet or roll of wire mesh or cloth (most often canvas or linen, but sometimes silk or another fabric). The flour produced by the mill was fed through or over the device, which was shaken by a mechanism (several were possible) taking power from the drive train leading from the water wheel to the millstones."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "953ebbba-fa88-3e56-91d5-2e295a95b952",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who sifts flour or meal."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "69ab90e1-5f60-336d-abe7-aaff482c643f",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A filter mechanism."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "230d0afd-64d5-46e1-aa57-1b892b2ee5ce",
                                "sense_id": "69ab90e1-5f60-336d-abe7-aaff482c643f",
                                "text": "This first bolter contains a screen of eight meshes to the inch and separates the hard particles, dirt or scale."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "26d4f597-c2ba-3a6d-aff0-e3858ad7f9ad",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An obscure athlete who wins an upset victory."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "67ee8f06-bc46-4e9e-a8f7-be491345f9e6",
                                "sense_id": "26d4f597-c2ba-3a6d-aff0-e3858ad7f9ad",
                                "text": "Last year he was eliminated by the bolter Jo-Wilfried Tsonga and this time he was beaten by the shining star, Fernando Verdasco."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "62492f19-534e-3e81-ad77-66526da5eb85",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A horse that wins at long odds."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3b522f06-3179-3a0f-a359-8cf5658e3385",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In team sports, a relatively little-known or inexperienced player who inspires the team to greater success."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "New-Zealand"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eafc2003-916e-3ee9-a249-69343de3cc56",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A member of a political party who does not support the party's nominee."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1fa041bc-c2d8-43b7-a391-e4546743f83c",
                                "sense_id": "eafc2003-916e-3ee9-a249-69343de3cc56",
                                "text": "The bolters from the Republican convention say, in their manifesto: \"Discontent and distress prevail to an extent never before known in the history of the country.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "84914634-ec52-342f-aef5-64273680621e",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A missed landing on an aircraft carrier; an aircraft that has made a missed landing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f7f5df21-b0ee-3358-ac23-387cbaaf6346",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A kind of fishing line; a boulter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "afe0717f-4f2c-3386-8c87-ff6887470ee6",
                        "entry_id": "a9ca2139-d5ec-333f-948f-43e1aedec127",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who equips a sport route by putting bolts in the rock."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
