            },
            {
                "entry_id": "3a750674-af53-36cd-8916-318c93e838bf",
                "word": "bolter",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9d98637e-74e1-42c0-afd1-f2f368af5679",
                        "entry_id": "3a750674-af53-36cd-8916-318c93e838bf",
                        "tags": [
                            "present",
                            "singular",
                            "third-person"
                        ],
                        "form": "bolters"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "d2d6a5c8-70fc-4500-8e0f-5df7261fbfa7",
                        "entry_id": "3a750674-af53-36cd-8916-318c93e838bf",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "present"
                        ],
                        "form": "boltering"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "f40acc69-0575-4a35-9c72-8d95a4b99432",
                        "entry_id": "3a750674-af53-36cd-8916-318c93e838bf",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "boltered"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1d664bab-1045-4148-a8ea-1025a8dccc49",
                        "entry_id": "3a750674-af53-36cd-8916-318c93e838bf",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "boltered"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d6c8d0e2-afcd-39bb-8767-ef4f3cc36524",
                        "entry_id": "3a750674-af53-36cd-8916-318c93e838bf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To smear or become smeared with a grimy substance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f08bf43-62ed-4408-aeb3-9eb4ff307a5b",
                                "sense_id": "d6c8d0e2-afcd-39bb-8767-ef4f3cc36524",
                                "text": "Methinks I see them with their boltered hair, Staring and grinning in thy gentle face, And in their ruthless hands their daggers drawn,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "08b388c6-f6f3-44e9-be26-84b38cb4b9bf",
                                "sense_id": "d6c8d0e2-afcd-39bb-8767-ef4f3cc36524",
                                "text": "Now I see 'tis true, For the blood-boltered Banquo smiles upon me, And points at them for his."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "406afe96-7167-49ab-a2ee-8c88b19c2032",
                                "sense_id": "d6c8d0e2-afcd-39bb-8767-ef4f3cc36524",
                                "text": "A saddler refused to black the linen lining of a harness-collar, though he had been told to do so, because the colouring would \"bolter\" the horse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "341e0a60-333a-4377-8c3e-f4fd993e3617",
                                "sense_id": "d6c8d0e2-afcd-39bb-8767-ef4f3cc36524",
                                "text": "She dashed hither and thither, never happy, always itching to be on somewhere else, with her eyebrows plucked to parentheses and her lotion-filled eyes boltering, looking as somebody said, like a peripatetic puff-ball."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7168539-2c8b-4c53-b139-280c5f51e9b1",
                                "sense_id": "d6c8d0e2-afcd-39bb-8767-ef4f3cc36524",
                                "text": "“The had seen me boltered in the blood of enemies\nwhen I battled and bound five beasts,\nraided a troll-nest and in the night-sea\nslaughtered sea-brutes.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "62c27d2d-0dad-4d44-be1a-d56b8c4b877b",
                                "sense_id": "d6c8d0e2-afcd-39bb-8767-ef4f3cc36524",
                                "text": "Then escaping from the foemen, boltered with the blood you shed, you, defiant, fearing no men, saved your honor and your head!."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "393b19c8-4046-3eb1-a0ff-32a24dcef520",
                        "entry_id": "3a750674-af53-36cd-8916-318c93e838bf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To sift or filter through a sieve or bolter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e27226db-518f-4419-9a0b-fbf2c64fa4a3",
                                "sense_id": "393b19c8-4046-3eb1-a0ff-32a24dcef520",
                                "text": "A thousand times the day, our Sieve is crowned; A thousand times 'tis drained: Let the Sieve once he strained, And, grain by grain, around Ye shall behold the ground Covered with folk, cast from the boltering Sieve."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e420711-01c1-4f65-abd7-eeebb294c170",
                                "sense_id": "393b19c8-4046-3eb1-a0ff-32a24dcef520",
                                "text": "Owing to the scarcity of food the old problem has latterly cropped up again whether, instead of baking white-bread, it would not be more practical to make bread of unboltered meal, since through the process of boltering the grain loses 20-30% of its nutritive value, according to the degree of milling."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0b37bcf-c84a-4a23-b475-b6f9935a365b",
                                "sense_id": "393b19c8-4046-3eb1-a0ff-32a24dcef520",
                                "text": "they were not themselves perhaps conscious how finely the foreign material must needs be boltered through a native sieve before it was palatable to English appetites, and, curiously as it may appear, for a couple of decades after the King's coming-in the hall-mark of your top-wit, your \"high-brow\" modern cant would name him, was not so much a Gallomania, as a particular veneration for \"the greatest man of the last age, Ben Johnson.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f7c3648b-a65c-3ace-bf35-ef8bec8ea3a6",
                        "entry_id": "3a750674-af53-36cd-8916-318c93e838bf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To fish using a bolter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a888c906-9e91-4847-891f-489efb97c69c",
                                "sense_id": "f7c3648b-a65c-3ace-bf35-ef8bec8ea3a6",
                                "text": "Those who are not boltering or spillering in the spring are crabbing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "08c66aa0-2ab4-4270-baa8-2c8bf7724133",
                                "sense_id": "f7c3648b-a65c-3ace-bf35-ef8bec8ea3a6",
                                "text": "Yes, as a place of residence our little town should commend itself to the wealthy leisured classes; and as for us poor working folk, why, we manage to get along tolerable well, thank 'e, what with our crabbing, and spiltering, and boltering, and trammelling, and teeling our little plats of land, and snaring a few rabbits now and again, and — this in your ear — maybe knocking over a pheasant or two at a particular time."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6ce0ceb7-552f-3906-b986-b49c8126c3dc",
                        "entry_id": "3a750674-af53-36cd-8916-318c93e838bf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To pound rapidly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3bb5b1d9-6250-4e60-af0a-303bf3c2b270",
                                "sense_id": "6ce0ceb7-552f-3906-b986-b49c8126c3dc",
                                "text": "In Elliotson v. Feetham, 2 Bingham's N.C., 134, in 1835, the plaintiff a physician resideing in the parish of St. George, Hanover Square, in the county of Middlesex, and possessed of a house for a term of years, sued the defendant in case for a nuisance in carrying on an iron-mongery factory, \"making divers large fires, and also divers loud, heavy, jarring, varying, agitating, hammering, and boltering sounds and noises.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d234e8f-a25a-4a39-a9ba-e35d7ff5d6bc",
                                "sense_id": "6ce0ceb7-552f-3906-b986-b49c8126c3dc",
                                "text": "The author refers the case of a teenager, eighteen years old, suffering from stuttering and boltering along with symptoms of anxiety, shakings and sweats."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f21452b3-f34c-4969-8e0c-9d0ea52df881",
                                "sense_id": "6ce0ceb7-552f-3906-b986-b49c8126c3dc",
                                "text": "I could put all that adolescent, everything-rides-on-this-putt crap behind me. Yet when I lay awake at night contemplating the months ahead, my heart would bolter and my breathing quicken."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "537d5597-8733-3647-94f0-45d833ddf17f",
                        "entry_id": "3a750674-af53-36cd-8916-318c93e838bf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To swim or turn sideways while eating."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of a whale"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc5d2a91-8983-460b-bd6d-02dd86634570",
                                "sense_id": "537d5597-8733-3647-94f0-45d833ddf17f",
                                "text": "Close observers of the habits of whales in more recent times however do not record this practice and it must be regarded as a fanciful belief which probably arose as Gunther (1949) suggests as a fisherman's explanation of the patches and their frequent association with boltering whales."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "beb793ed-0ede-436a-b3b8-1ced2f1e6e72",
                                "sense_id": "537d5597-8733-3647-94f0-45d833ddf17f",
                                "text": "Concerning with feeding habits of baleen whales, it has been also known that they follow to two different ways to collect the food organisms, say, “skimming” and “swallowing ” or “gulping ” by boltering the body while feeding,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f357c3d-ac5c-4d79-975d-466aec10f5d4",
                                "sense_id": "537d5597-8733-3647-94f0-45d833ddf17f",
                                "text": "May be seen \"breaching,\" propelling the body about halfway out of the water, then falling back with a huge splash; \"Skyhopping,\" rising vertically out of the water apparently to visually scan the area; and \"boltering,\" lying on its side while waving a pectoral fin in the air."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "28bacb25-41f4-3a31-a835-35fd3441d544",
                        "entry_id": "3a750674-af53-36cd-8916-318c93e838bf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To miss a landing on an aircraft carrier by failing to catch the arresting gear wires with the aircraft's tailhook."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "724bd78a-543b-449f-93e4-50094d65b613",
                                "sense_id": "28bacb25-41f4-3a31-a835-35fd3441d544",
                                "text": "Commander Kleemann came back and boltered again on his second attempt. lt is unheard of for him to bolter twice in a row. Then on his third attempt he got aboard with an OK three-wire trap."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d361e1b2-e798-4c6f-adb7-c65436dc955c",
                                "sense_id": "28bacb25-41f4-3a31-a835-35fd3441d544",
                                "text": "In the Diamondback's ready room, a tailhook bolt hangs by a string from the ceiling over one pilot's seat; he was the last to \"bolter\" that day, meaning he missed the wires while landing and had to make another pass."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ef82aed-899b-4c9a-b615-13c1f77c0e65",
                                "sense_id": "28bacb25-41f4-3a31-a835-35fd3441d544",
                                "text": "Tomcat 209 had one engine out, and if his tailhook failed to engage an arrestor wire, he wouldn't have the power necessary to complete a touch-and-go and would bolter off the forward end of the flight deck again."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0dde394-ab64-40f9-89c7-b762bdde1f45",
                                "sense_id": "28bacb25-41f4-3a31-a835-35fd3441d544",
                                "text": "The majority had bet I'd come down on the 2 wire, or, worse yet, knowing I did not want to bolter, the 1 wire."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
